Spec: WeekTheme entity

Purpose:
  The WeekTheme entity: the theme of one calendar week of one CourseRealization, a single free-text title such as
  `Introduction to gradient descent`. It is per realization, not per Semester, so two groups of the same Course can
  theme the same week differently, and it labels the week rather than changing what is taught in it. A view-less,
  route-less package used by ../realizations/realizations.sdd, whose weekly view owns the affordances that create,
  edit and remove one.

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd

Must:
  A WeekTheme has a reference to exactly one CourseRealization stored as a plain id, the Monday that starts its week
    and a non-empty free-text title. The Monday identifies the week on its own, so no ISO year or week number is
    stored and a Semester spanning New Year cannot give two of its weeks the same number.
  `week_start` is a Monday, since it identifies a week the way /aikana.sdd defines one; any other weekday is rejected.
  The CourseRealization reference is declared as a foreign key, so the database enforces it and cascades a removed
    CourseRealization to its WeekThemes; no service hand-deletes WeekThemes.
  At most one WeekTheme exists per week and CourseRealization; a second theme for the same week is rejected with
    @DuplicateWeekThemeError, and the same pair carries a unique index on the table as the database-level backstop.
  @WeekThemeService.add_week_theme validates that the CourseRealization id exists (through
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's ports.py, per ../architecture.sdd) and that the title is non-empty, rejecting
    with @UnknownRealizationError or @InvalidWeekThemeError before storage.
  @WeekThemeService.update_week_theme applies the same checks, ignoring the WeekTheme being edited when looking for
    the week it already themes, and keeps the CourseRealization the WeekTheme already belongs to; it rejects an
    unknown id with @UnknownWeekThemeError.
  @WeekThemeService.delete_week_theme removes a WeekTheme and leaves the realization's other themes untouched,
    rejecting an unknown id with @UnknownWeekThemeError.
  @WeekThemeService.list_week_themes returns one CourseRealization's themes ordered by week, which is what
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly view-model reads once for both the title each week renders and the id
    its dialogs address the stored theme by.
  @WeekThemeRepository in ./ports.py exposes get, list themes for a CourseRealization, and add, update and delete
    operations backing ./services.py.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist.

Must not:
  This package must not gain a view.py or routes.py: a WeekTheme is created, edited and removed only through
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly view, so the feature's affordances and routes stay owned there.

Tasks:
  [x] Implement @WeekTheme in ./domain.py, and ./ports.py, ./services.py and ./repository_sqlite.py with
    @WeekThemeService validating through ../realizations/realizations.sdd's ports.py, per ../architecture.sdd
  [x] Show the theme in ../realizations/realizations.sdd's Week cell and add its create, edit and delete routes there
  [x] Expose list, read and token-gated write tools for WeekThemes in ../mcp_server/mcp_server.sdd